I(37,[40,42,44,46],'construction said to work',[34,36,38,40],'1427–1464;1484–1519;1539–1598;1618–1655','F^f=ϖ','For A=O_K, [K:Q_p]=ef and residue field F_q, a rank-one A-linear Dieudonné module splits into f rank-one A components; F has exponents0≤r_ν≤e, F^f=ϖ and dim G=Σr_ν. Dimension one means one exponent1 and the others0.','Ranks over W and A must be separated: rank_W=eΣrank_A=ef. This classification assumes the displayed field/base and semilinear action.','agrees','The notes correctly isolate the omitted e and shift-direction risks rather than changing the formulas.')
I(38,[46,48],'computation',[40,42],'1618–1655;1672–1699','ϖ=ϖ′','An A-linear nonzero map between the rank-one isocrystals exists only for the same ϖ, and then all maps are scalar; integral homomorphisms are the scalar lattice cut out by component valuation inequalities.','With cumulative exponents s_j, the condition is v(v₀)+s_j−s′_j≥0; hence v(v₀)≥max_j(s′_j−s_j), including j=0.','agrees','The direction-dependent A or πA formula in dimension one is checked from the displayed indexing, not from an arbitrary modern convention.')
