I(40,[50],'reading question',[44],'1722–1753','Ω/pΩ','The dimension-one Hodge quotient is compared with Ω/pΩ and with M_ν reduced to the residue field; a proposed tensor construction relates G₀(A) to general Ω.','For ramification index e>1, Ω/pΩ has residue-field length e, while the cotangent line has length1. Ω/πΩ is a candidate reading, not an emendation. Contravariance also affects the proposed tensor construction.','agrees','The discrepancy is mathematical evidence for checking the ink, not evidence that the transcriber chose the wrong glyph.')
I(41,[41,43,45,47,49,52],'other',[35,37,39,41,43,45,47],'1465–1483;1520–1538;1599–1617;1656–1671;1700–1721;1754–1781;1812–1830','jets d’ordre k','Reused differential-manifold text: chart-independent contact, jet composition, coordinate polynomial models, truncations, jet bundles of sections, symbol exact sequence and base change.','For origin-preserving polynomial jets R^p→R^q, the dimension is q(binomial(p+k,k)−1). Jet composition uses b∘c∘a^{-1} for source change a and target change b. Iterated derivative embeddings need the characteristic-zero/differentiability framework.','agrees','The notes identify the omitted constant-term subtraction, reversed action and base-domain issues. Typed order is47→45→43→[missing p80]→41→39→37→35.')
