I(44,[51],'unpursued implication',[46],'1782–1811','πA muni de puissances divisées','For a mixed-characteristic DVR with v_π(p)=e, the canonical rational divided powers π^n/n! lie in πA for every n exactly when e≤p−1.','PD stability and PD nilpotence are different: at e=p−1, v_π(π^{p^r}/(p^r)!)=1, so the divided powers do not tend to zero modulo π².','understates','The earlier note notices the ramification issue; the boundary nilpotence obstruction is made explicit in this run.')
I(45,[53,55],'open on the pages',[48,50],'1831–1854;1873–1889','Il resterait à prouver','The page distinguishes isogeny-level uniqueness from existence, and asks whether the crystalline lattice M and the lattice D*(G) agree, equivalently whether the exponent α in the tangent/cotangent comparison is zero.','If t_G=π^{-α}Ω∨, then ω_G=π^αΩ and Ω=π^{-α}ω_G. The other displayed sign is inconsistent. Rational admissibility does not settle this precise integral equality.','agrees','The note correctly retains the open integral comparison and does not identify every filtered isocrystal with a lift.')
